        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-27638",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan\u2061x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- **II.** The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$\n- **III.** The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan\u2061x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,\u2026,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."
      },
