        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-27660",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{\u03c0}{2} + \u03c0n$.\n- **II.** The range of the function is $y \u2208 (-\\frac{\u03c0}{2}, \\frac{\u03c0}{2})$.\n- **III.** The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = n\u03c0$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Tangent has vertical asymptotes at pi/2+n*pi and range all real numbers. Its domain excludes pi/2+n*pi, rather than n*pi. Only I is true."
      },
