        ":question/id": "c5a3a079-0ec8-5b33-84d2-568517288149",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29608",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x)=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x+2n\\pi ).$\n\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-1,1].$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan\u2061x.$\n\n![](images/31/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan\u2061x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan\u2061(x+2n\\pi )=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi )=tan\u2061(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan\u2061x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$"
